{
  "schema_version": 3,
  "$comment": "Synthetic WP3.2 qualification, not experimental calibration. Same Exercise 4.15 balances; mu=mu_mechanistic*exp(theta*S/(S+S_ref)). S_ref=Ks=1 g/L is a fixed feature scale. theta=0 is exactly neutral; |theta|<=ln(2) is a design restriction giving a multiplier between 1/2 and 2 for S>=0. Domain S<=10 g/L and X<=5 g/L follows the nominal sterile-feed yield invariant. Formal MW=1000 g/mol makes mmol/L numerically equal to g/L only in this benchmark. The hybrid rules explicitly convert concentration [mmol/L] to [g/L] using each formal molecular weight divided by 1000 mmol/mol before applying mass-basis equations and domain bounds.",
